  "brief": "DoorDash is acquiring Instacart in a $17 billion deal to expand its grocery delivery business.\n\nDoorDash / Instacart (Announced): DoorDash to Acquire Instacart. DoorDash is acquiring Instacart in a $17 billion deal [1, 2, 3]. The deal is for Instacart, a US rival in the grocery delivery business [1, 2, 3]. The acquisition is expected to expand DoorDash's grocery delivery business [1, 2, 3].\nMarvell / Lumentum (Rumored): Marvell and Lumentum Deal Rumors. Marvell is reportedly in advanced talks to acquire Lumentum for its AI optics business [15, 17, 18]. The deal is said to be worth $221B, but no terms have been confirmed yet [16, 20]. The acquisition would be one of the 10 largest tech and telecom deals ever [19]. The deal is currently in the rumored stage, with no official confirmation from the companies [13, 14, 17].\nThrive Holdings / ADT (Announced): Thrive Holdings to Acquire ADT. Thrive Holdings is acquiring ADT in an all-cash deal [21, 22, 23]. The deal is valued at $15.3 billion [22, 24]. The acquisition is expected to be completed soon [25, 26].\nVaisala / Atmo (Completed): Vaisala Acquires Atmo. Vaisala has acquired Atmo, a company that provides AI weather products [27, 28]. The deal is now completed [27, 28].\nTrian-led group / Wendy's (Announced): Trian-led Group Bids for Wendy's. A Trian-led group has bid $1.4 billion to take Wendy's private [29, 30]. The deal is part of a larger trend of private equity firms taking companies private [31].\nIntel / Classiq (Announced): Intel Acquires Classiq. Intel is acquiring Classiq, a quantum software company [32, 33, 34]. The deal is valued at $2.3 billion [34, 36, 37]. The acquisition is expected to set a record for a quantum computing deal [37, 38].\nEnerpac / SFE Group (Completed): Enerpac Acquires SFE Group. Enerpac has acquired SFE Group [39, 40]. Three executives must buy shares as Enerpac closes its SFE Group acquisition [40].\nUFP Industries / Texas pallet maker (Announced): UFP Industries Acquires Texas Pallet Maker. UFP Industries has acquired a Texas pallet maker [41, 42]. The deal is the company's third acquisition this year [41]. The acquisition expands UFP Industries' pallet manufacturing network [42].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Axalta Coating Systems Ltd. is merging with Akzo Nobel, offering cost-saving potential, according to Ariel Global Fund [43].\n- GE Vernova has strengthened its grid energy business after a $9 billion acquisition deal [44].\n- Monte dei Paschi investors have rejected a defence plan, clearing the path for Intesa's €35 billion takeover [45].",
